# Cursor Rules — Forge v3

## The reference standard
Before ANY UI work, open config/design_constitution.py and check:
- REFERENCE_SITES: Composio, Hex, Riff, Linear, Vercel — these are the bar
- STATIC_DESIGN_LAWS: 7 timeless laws
- ANTI_SLOP_RULES: 38 specific patterns to avoid
- LIVING_KNOWLEDGE: current best tools (auto-updated by knowledge_updater agent)

Ask: "Does this look like it belongs on composio.dev or linear.app?"
If not, it's not good enough.

---

## Immutable vs Living sections

### IMMUTABLE — never change, agents never touch
- config/design_constitution.py → all sections EXCEPT LIVING_KNOWLEDGE
  (STATIC_DESIGN_LAWS, ANTI_SLOP_RULES, DESIGN_PERSONALITIES, DESIGN_CRITIQUE_RUBRIC,
   COMPONENT_QUALITY_CHECKLIST, REFERENCE_SITES, agent system prompts, DesignTokens class)
- config/electronhub.py → LLM client + routing
- config/docker-compose.yml → infrastructure
- pyproject.toml → Python deps
- All Python infra (Redis patterns, PostgreSQL, Temporal)

### LIVING — agents update these
- config/design_constitution.py → LIVING_KNOWLEDGE section ONLY
  (trending libraries, winning concepts, stack recommendations)
- Agent: agents/python/infra/knowledge_updater.py
- Run: `python agents/python/infra/knowledge_updater.py`
- Schedule: before each hackathon cycle, or weekly

---

## Python rules

### ElectronHub — the one rule
```python
from config.electronhub import complete, complete_json, embed
# NEVER: from openai import AsyncOpenAI + direct instantiation
```

### Design tier uses higher temperature automatically
```python
# These use 0.7 temperature (creativity)
await complete(task="design-system-create", ...)
await complete(task="generate-color-palette", ...)
await complete(task="critique-design", ...)

# These use lower temperature (precision)
await complete(task="generate-component", ...)
await complete(task="fix-lint-error", ...)
```

### Every design agent loads LIVING_KNOWLEDGE
```python
from config.design_constitution import LIVING_KNOWLEDGE, SYSTEM_PROMPT_DESIGN_AGENT
# Include current_stack in prompts so agent uses correct tools
```

---

## TypeScript (browser layer only)
```typescript
// ALWAYS route Stagehand through ElectronHub
const stagehand = new Stagehand({
  modelClientOptions: {
    apiKey: process.env.ELECTRONHUB_API_KEY,
    baseURL: "https://api.electronhub.ai/v1",
  },
});
```

---

## Frontend standards (Composio/Linear quality)
```tsx
// Hover = background-color change, NOT opacity
className="hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors duration-[120ms]"
// NOT: "hover:opacity-70"

// All states via CVA
const variants = cva("...", {
  variants: { state: { default: "...", loading: "...", error: "...", disabled: "opacity-40 cursor-not-allowed" }}
})

// AI streaming = Vercel AI SDK (never custom)
import { useChat } from "ai/react"
```

---

## Redis keys (immutable schema)
```
hackathon:{id}:brief            HackathonBrief
hackathon:{id}:api_contract     ApiContract (published immediately by Architect)
task:{id}:{agent_id}            {status, data}
checkpoint:{id}:{type}          "pending" | {approved: true}
```
